-- title:
--   Base change of a bialgebra cokernel along R → S
-- statement:
--   Let $R$ be a commutative ring, $S$ a commutative $R$-algebra, and let $B$, $C$, $H$ be commutative rings carrying $R$-bialgebra structures. Given $R$-bialgebra homomorphisms $\psi \colon B \to C$ and $q \colon C \to H$ with $q$ surjective and such that the kernel of $q$, as a ring homomorphism, equals the ideal of $C$ generated by the image under $\psi$ of the kernel of the counit $\varepsilon_B \colon B \to R$ (i.e. $\ker q = \mathrm{Ideal.map}\,\psi\,(\ker \varepsilon_B)$), and given in addition a commutative ring $T$ with an $S$-bialgebra structure together with a surjective $S$-bialgebra homomorphism $\pi \colon S \otimes_R C \to T$ whose kernel is the ideal of $S \otimes_R C$ generated by the image, under the bialgebra map $\mathrm{id}_S \otimes \psi \colon S \otimes_R B \to S \otimes_R C$, of the kernel of the counit $\varepsilon_{S \otimes_R B} \colon S \otimes_R B \to S$, the conclusion is that there exists an isomorphism $e \colon T \xrightarrow{\sim} S \otimes_R H$ of $S$-bialgebras such that $e(\pi(x)) = (\mathrm{id}_S \otimes q)(x)$ for every $x \in S \otimes_R C$.
--
--   This is the statement that the bialgebra cokernel of $\psi$ (the quotient of $C$ by the ideal generated by the augmentation ideal of $B$) commutes with base change along $R \to S$, with no flatness hypothesis; the hypotheses are shaped so as to match the output of the construction of such a quotient over $R$ and over $S$. It is used in the analysis of torus quotients attached to modular curves, in [`ModularCurve.exists_hopfCokernel_free_finrank_eq_pow_of_finPtsWitness`](thm.html#ModularCurve.exists_hopfCokernel_free_finrank_eq_pow_of_finPtsWitness) and [`ModularCurve.nonempty_bialgEquiv_baseChange_residueField_torusQuotient_one_addMonoidAlgebra_of_finPtsWitness`](thm.html#ModularCurve.nonempty_bialgEquiv_baseChange_residueField_torusQuotient_one_addMonoidAlgebra_of_finPtsWitness).
